# Aura Music — Cloudflare Pages headers.
#
# Two Cloudflare behaviours drive the shape of this file. Both are documented at
# https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/
#
# 1. A header set by more than one matching rule is JOINED with a comma, it does
#    not override. So a blanket `Cache-Control` on `/*` poisons every narrower
#    rule: `no-cache, must-revalidate` + `public, max-age=31536000, immutable`
#    is a single contradictory value, and `no-cache` wins. A narrower rule has
#    to DETACH the header first with `! Cache-Control`, then set its own.
#
# 2. A splat `*` is greedy and matches `/` as well as any other character. So
#    `/*.png` also matches `/assets/logo-B6rNPeia.png`. That means the
#    extension rules must come BEFORE `/assets/*`, not after, or they would
#    detach the immutable rule and downgrade hashed assets to a week.
#
# Order below is therefore: broadest first, `/assets/*` last so it has the final
# say on anything Vite emitted.

# Default: HTML and anything unhashed revalidates, so a deploy is picked up on
# the next request. Security headers apply everywhere.
/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache, must-revalidate
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN

# Stable-name files copied from public/ (logos, icons, the vinyl mark). These do
# NOT carry a content hash, so a year would pin a stale logo after a redesign.
# A week is long enough to matter and short enough to recover from.
/*.png
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800

/*.svg
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800

/*.webp
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800

/*.jpg
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800

/*.ico
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800

# The catalogue manifest is fetched by the admin pipeline and can change on any
# upload. Five minutes keeps it fresh without hammering the bucket.
/manifest.json
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300

# Vite emits content-hashed filenames here (main-B6rNPeia.js, dm-sans-latin-
# CwMReqGs.woff2, about-logo-C-N56Vop.jpg, ...). The hash changes whenever the
# bytes change, so these are safe to cache for a year and never revalidate.
# Deliberately LAST: it must win over the extension rules above, which also
# match hashed images.
/assets/*
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
